\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
\ src/fence.fam — shared RISC-V fence macros for the device modules.
\
\ The node has no zicsr (no interrupts); every device is polled, and correctness
\ depends on ordering MMIO writes before a QueueNotify and ordering used-ring/DMA
\ reads after the device completes.  Both src/disk.fam and src/net.fam need these,
\ and `:M` redefinition is rejected by the compiler, so they live here once and are
\ compiled FIRST.  Each module is then independently testable by prepending this
\ file, e.g.  ./tools/fam --test src/fence.fam src/net.fam
\ ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

:M fence_io 0F00500F , ;           \ fence iorw,ow   (order MMIO writes before QueueNotify)
:M fence_r  0F002002 , ;           \ fence r,r       (order reads after device DMA)
